WEBVTT

00:02.877 --> 00:05.963
<i>Long time ago, a Luminescent Baby
was born in China.</i>

00:05.964 --> 00:08.466
<i>People born with Quirks
increased day by day</i>

00:09.259 --> 00:10.634
<i>and created a super-powered society</i>

00:10.635 --> 00:13.763
<i>where 80% of the world's population
possesses some form of a Quirk.</i>

00:14.347 --> 00:15.931
<i>I, Koichi Haimawari,</i>

00:15.932 --> 00:17.684
<i>was born with a Quirk too.</i>

00:18.393 --> 00:19.852
<i>By day, I'm a university student.</i>

00:19.853 --> 00:21.104
<i>But at night...</i>

00:22.021 --> 00:23.314
<i>I was spending time</i>

00:23.898 --> 00:26.651
<i>doing charitable work in my neighborhood
as the mysterious Nice Guy.</i>

00:27.652 --> 00:30.946
<i>Due to an incident I came across,</i>

00:30.947 --> 00:33.783
<i>I met a dangerous old man
named Knuckleduster.</i>

00:34.534 --> 00:37.287
<i>And I was kind of forced
into taking on Hero-like duties.</i>

00:38.371 --> 00:41.248
<i>Now I'm an anonymous vigilante.</i>

00:41.249 --> 00:43.167
<i>The Crawler.</i>

00:43.168 --> 00:46.462
<i>As vigilantes, our goal
is to prevent crimes.</i>

00:46.463 --> 00:48.131
<i>We are unlicensed Heroes.</i>

00:48.715 --> 00:50.382
<i>Unlicensed Heroes are illegal.</i>

00:50.383 --> 00:53.887
<i>So, basically, we're violating
the rules a little bit,</i>

00:54.888 --> 00:56.555
<i>but we're working in the shadows</i>

00:56.556 --> 00:58.349
<i>for the sake of society.</i>

01:03.521 --> 01:06.858
It's true that a lot has happened
these last few years.

01:07.859 --> 01:10.820
But I don't think all of it has been bad.

01:12.405 --> 01:16.326
Because now, I can take time
to be with my family like this,

01:17.285 --> 01:19.537
and I've also been reexamining myself.

01:20.497 --> 01:23.708
I have a hobby too. And I have friends.

01:24.334 --> 01:27.253
I'm leading a life
that's a lot better than before.

01:29.130 --> 01:33.091
I should've done this a lot sooner.

01:33.092 --> 01:36.304
Oguro-san. Sir.

01:37.388 --> 01:39.181
Do you have a minute?

01:39.182 --> 01:41.099
The doctor would like to speak with you.

01:41.100 --> 01:42.143
Sure.

01:42.852 --> 01:43.685
EXAM ROOM

01:43.686 --> 01:46.021
This is about your wife's condition.

01:46.022 --> 01:49.776
Currently, she's in decline...

02:10.964 --> 02:12.924
It may be hard to accept,

02:13.508 --> 02:17.137
but her condition is...

03:49.520 --> 03:50.938
IDOL

03:50.939 --> 03:52.898
AN OBJECT OF ADMIRATION OR WORSHIP

03:52.899 --> 03:54.442
CELEBRITIES WHO CHARM AUDIENCES
WITH THEIR PERSONALITIES

03:58.905 --> 04:01.407
- Bye.
- See you.

04:04.285 --> 04:06.745
Do you know this girl?

04:06.746 --> 04:10.082
This is a picture of her
when she was in middle school.

04:10.083 --> 04:12.126
Her hairstyle is different now.

04:12.710 --> 04:14.628
- Is he hitting on her?
- In front of the school?

04:14.629 --> 04:16.588
He looks scary.

04:16.589 --> 04:20.300
He's looking for a girl with
"one eye covered" and "short hair", but...

04:20.301 --> 04:21.885
Hey!

04:21.886 --> 04:23.679
Isn't that Hachisuka?

04:23.680 --> 04:25.180
Did she do something?

04:25.181 --> 04:29.059
I don't know what's going on,
but I'll let her know just in case.

04:29.060 --> 04:31.895
- Do you have her number?
- Hey there.

04:31.896 --> 04:35.525
- We received complaints about you.
- What are you doing here?

04:37.193 --> 04:38.861
Oh he's being kicked out.

04:39.529 --> 04:41.364
I guess it's all okay now.

04:42.824 --> 04:43.992
Oh?

04:51.499 --> 04:53.333
Hey there.

04:53.334 --> 04:55.420
Are you looking for Hachisuka?

04:57.380 --> 05:00.382
Why are you looking for her?

05:00.383 --> 05:02.677
It seems like you're
into some shady business.

05:03.344 --> 05:05.679
I'm just a messenger.

05:05.680 --> 05:08.599
I don't know if the business
is shady or not.

05:09.809 --> 05:11.936
Oh, you're just an errand boy?

05:13.896 --> 05:17.734
I guess it's useless to waste
my time on an errand boy.

05:19.485 --> 05:21.321
What should I do...

05:22.780 --> 05:25.532
Hey! What the hell are you doing?

05:25.533 --> 05:27.117
Stop trying to cause trouble!

05:27.118 --> 05:30.121
You're the one that's causing trouble.

05:34.625 --> 05:35.835
BEE KILLER

05:40.465 --> 05:41.632
Damn it.

05:48.181 --> 05:49.682
Soga! Over here!

06:03.029 --> 06:04.488
What's going on, Soga?

06:04.489 --> 06:06.698
Did you get yourself into trouble again?

06:06.699 --> 06:09.117
It's none of your guys' business.

06:09.118 --> 06:11.078
Come on. Don't be like that.

06:11.079 --> 06:13.998
That's right. You can't have fun
all by yourself.

06:14.582 --> 06:16.584
It seems like things
are getting pretty interesting.

06:24.300 --> 06:27.427
Your doctor tried to scare me
the other day.

06:27.428 --> 06:31.432
But doctors aren't always right.

06:31.974 --> 06:33.101
Look at me, for example.

06:33.601 --> 06:36.103
People gave up on me countless times.

06:36.104 --> 06:37.854
Tama...

06:37.855 --> 06:39.482
Come back

06:40.399 --> 06:41.901
before it gets dark.

06:42.401 --> 06:44.570
Your dad is worried about you.

06:45.947 --> 06:48.324
Leave Tama up to me.

06:49.242 --> 06:52.537
Don't worry.
Everything is going as planned.

06:53.704 --> 06:56.039
RECEPTION

06:56.040 --> 06:58.416
<i>Doctor Yamada.</i>

06:58.417 --> 07:00.627
<i>Please come to exam room 12.</i>

07:00.628 --> 07:01.546
Hey.

07:02.171 --> 07:03.714
What are you doing waiting here?

07:04.423 --> 07:05.507
Old Man,

07:05.508 --> 07:09.262
the receptionist told me
that there's no patient named Kuroiwa.

07:10.596 --> 07:13.390
That business card is only for you
to get in touch with me.

07:13.391 --> 07:15.308
Then what's your real name?

07:15.309 --> 07:17.728
Do you really have
a "hospitalized family member"?

07:20.356 --> 07:25.652
Hey, you shouldn't meddle
in other people's business.

07:25.653 --> 07:28.322
It's a little too late for that,
don't you think?

07:30.158 --> 07:31.908
I looked into the bee user.

07:31.909 --> 07:35.203
I tracked down her school
based on the uniform she was wearing.

07:35.204 --> 07:37.081
And I ended up getting attacked.

07:39.375 --> 07:42.878
<i>She asked me what
my business was with Hachisuka.</i>

07:42.879 --> 07:46.673
<i>That's probably her alias. She's probably
not in the school registry either.</i>

07:46.674 --> 07:49.843
But an alias is still useful intel.

07:49.844 --> 07:50.761
Good work.

07:51.304 --> 07:53.222
That school was a local
private school, huh?

07:53.723 --> 07:55.766
You're getting involved
with dangerous people.

07:56.350 --> 07:58.477
Are they aware of this?

07:58.478 --> 08:02.482
Oh, are you worried about Koichi and Pop?

08:03.441 --> 08:07.235
There's no need for them
to get involved in this.

08:07.236 --> 08:10.405
If you do flashy things
and attract attention,

08:10.406 --> 08:12.575
new leads will eventually
fall into our laps.

08:13.451 --> 08:14.826
I'm your decoy?

08:14.827 --> 08:16.411
You're the right man for this situation.

08:16.412 --> 08:17.537
Whoa!

08:17.538 --> 08:18.748
Fist Geezer!

08:19.624 --> 08:23.793
Then, do you want to go around
dressed up like All Might?

08:23.794 --> 08:25.713
You've got to be kidding me.

08:26.380 --> 08:29.509
Exactly. So, you get my point.

08:33.763 --> 08:35.180
Soga.

08:35.181 --> 08:38.141
I know you're being really
stubborn about this.

08:38.142 --> 08:41.478
But I don't think you should
get involved with this any further.

08:41.479 --> 08:43.856
Both with this drug and the Fist Geezer.

08:47.151 --> 08:49.361
The drug is one thing,

08:49.362 --> 08:51.696
but the Fist Geezer
is nothing but trouble.

08:51.697 --> 08:53.907
He's absolutely crazy.

08:53.908 --> 08:55.784
Yeah.

08:55.785 --> 08:58.162
Oh! Soga-san!

08:58.871 --> 09:00.163
Long time no see!

09:00.164 --> 09:01.874
Why are you greeting him?

09:02.792 --> 09:05.336
How are you?
How's the injury from the other day?

09:07.046 --> 09:09.047
Your outfit is revealing as always!

09:09.048 --> 09:10.132
Shut up!

09:12.927 --> 09:15.929
I don't know if you're Nice Guy
or the Cruller,

09:15.930 --> 09:20.183
but how can you be so friendly
with someone who once beat you up?

09:20.184 --> 09:21.101
Well...

09:21.102 --> 09:23.813
A lot has happened since then.

09:24.397 --> 09:25.815
Right, Soga-san?

09:28.067 --> 09:29.193
Oh?

09:31.070 --> 09:32.863
- Slut!
- Shut up!

09:36.576 --> 09:37.952
I'm home!

09:39.870 --> 09:41.747
Hey, Mom, listen to this.

09:42.748 --> 09:45.292
There was a stalker
that came looking for me

09:45.293 --> 09:47.460
at school today.

09:47.461 --> 09:48.588
So scary, huh?

09:52.758 --> 09:53.842
Oh, by the way, Dad,

09:53.843 --> 09:56.596
this credit card has been maxed out now.

09:57.263 --> 09:58.722
I'll return it to you.

09:58.723 --> 10:01.058
The credit limit was pretty pathetic.

10:01.851 --> 10:03.019
All right,

10:03.644 --> 10:04.978
let's watch TV.

10:04.979 --> 10:06.313
A HIGH SCHOOL GIRL FOUND COLLAPSED
ON THE STREET. WHAT HAPPENED TO HER?

10:06.314 --> 10:08.023
- Let's eat.
- <i>Onto the next news.</i>

10:08.024 --> 10:10.775
<i>Today, there was a report
that a high school girl was found</i>

10:10.776 --> 10:13.528
<i>on the street two kilometers
from East Naruhata Station</i>

10:13.529 --> 10:16.699
<i>in Tokyo, Naruhata City.</i>

10:17.199 --> 10:18.908
<i>When officials found her...</i>

10:18.909 --> 10:22.455
I'm getting a little tired of living here.

10:24.123 --> 10:26.917
Maybe it's time to move.

10:57.615 --> 10:59.241
I won't let you get away.

11:09.043 --> 11:10.127
Performance request?

11:12.338 --> 11:13.589
For what?

11:14.256 --> 11:16.299
I received a message through my blog.

11:16.300 --> 11:20.554
It's an offer to attend an event
on the roof of a department store.

11:21.806 --> 11:24.100
Wow! You're like a real idol.

11:25.142 --> 11:27.060
But what should I do?

11:27.061 --> 11:30.522
Objectively speaking, I'm just

11:30.523 --> 11:33.275
someone who sings
and performs on the street.

11:34.485 --> 11:36.986
<i>I guess she's aware of that.</i>

11:36.987 --> 11:39.989
Oh, come on. You have lots of fans.

11:39.990 --> 11:43.202
But I'll be compared
with other performers.

11:44.120 --> 11:47.247
If I make a mistake on such a big stage,
I'll disappoint my fans,

11:47.248 --> 11:48.666
and they might leave me.

11:49.917 --> 11:51.335
Then you can decline.

11:52.002 --> 11:53.003
But...

11:53.712 --> 11:55.965
I might never get an opportunity
like this ever again.

11:57.133 --> 11:58.426
<i>So, she wants to perform.</i>

11:59.009 --> 12:00.886
Koichi, what do you think I should do?

12:01.679 --> 12:02.513
Me?

12:04.849 --> 12:06.766
Let's see.

12:06.767 --> 12:08.476
You'll do just fine.

12:08.477 --> 12:10.896
Stop trying to make me feel better!

12:11.480 --> 12:12.939
Maybe you should decline.

12:12.940 --> 12:15.359
You should support me!

12:16.152 --> 12:17.569
Master, what do you think?

12:17.570 --> 12:20.531
Hey! I didn't ask the old man
for his opinion!

12:21.157 --> 12:24.910
Why don't you just go and do what you can?

12:26.495 --> 12:27.496
Koichi.

12:28.122 --> 12:29.457
Help her out.

12:32.793 --> 12:34.170
Good luck.

12:38.924 --> 12:40.008
What was that?

12:40.009 --> 12:41.926
Master is so normal that it's weird.

12:41.927 --> 12:44.471
Concentrate on my problem!

12:44.472 --> 12:46.181
Oh, right.

12:46.182 --> 12:49.185
I'll help out with whatever I can.

12:50.352 --> 12:51.395
Therefore,

12:52.146 --> 12:54.814
I asked Makoto-senpai for advice!

12:54.815 --> 12:56.609
Leave everything up to me!

12:58.611 --> 13:00.196
Let's do this, Pop-chan.

13:02.072 --> 13:04.241
Who's that? I don't know
anyone by that name.

13:05.409 --> 13:06.452
I see.

13:09.914 --> 13:12.248
Why did you leak my identity to her?

13:12.249 --> 13:13.875
I didn't leak anything.

13:13.876 --> 13:16.669
But she has good intuition.

13:16.670 --> 13:20.423
She found out a lot about us
ever since that bus incident.

13:20.424 --> 13:22.383
By the way, where's Master Knuckle?

13:22.384 --> 13:25.221
He left a while ago.

13:25.971 --> 13:28.139
Now, now, don't be so upset.

13:28.140 --> 13:30.059
Can you please hear me out?

13:31.101 --> 13:32.770
First of all,

13:33.479 --> 13:35.480
regardless of this event,

13:35.481 --> 13:37.732
I promise not to tell anyone

13:37.733 --> 13:41.194
about your guys' "masked activities".

13:41.195 --> 13:43.613
I will protect my sources.

13:43.614 --> 13:45.406
Second,

13:45.407 --> 13:49.035
if you allow me to play a bigger role
in helping you out,

13:49.036 --> 13:51.162
it will become a part of my work.

13:51.163 --> 13:55.251
I won't do anything to interfere
with our "professional relationship".

13:56.460 --> 13:59.003
I have no idea what you're talking about.

13:59.004 --> 14:00.838
And last but not least,

14:00.839 --> 14:04.176
I hate to say so myself,
but I'm pretty capable.

14:05.636 --> 14:07.554
If there's anything you want to do,

14:07.555 --> 14:09.348
feel free to ask me for help!

14:10.015 --> 14:13.561
Of course, if you already have
someone reliable, I won't force you.

14:14.812 --> 14:16.020
What do you say?

14:16.021 --> 14:17.481
Someone reliable...

14:18.315 --> 14:19.358
SOMEONE RELIABLE

14:19.900 --> 14:21.192
What is it?

14:21.193 --> 14:22.360
SOMEONE RELIABLE

14:22.361 --> 14:23.904
SOMEONE UNRELIABLE

14:25.072 --> 14:27.115
I will reluctantly agree.

14:27.116 --> 14:28.491
That's a wise decision.

14:28.492 --> 14:31.954
All right. Let's review
our current situation.

14:32.538 --> 14:34.372
According to the email you forwarded,

14:34.373 --> 14:37.542
you were invited to perform
at the department store's free live event.

14:37.543 --> 14:38.459
MARUKANE

14:38.460 --> 14:40.461
<i>It'll be located at the event area</i>

14:40.462 --> 14:43.090
<i>on the roof of Marukane Department Store,
East Naruhata Branch.</i>

14:43.716 --> 14:45.758
<i>The area where the event will be held</i>

14:45.759 --> 14:47.802
<i>has the capacity to host 300 guests.</i>

14:47.803 --> 14:50.514
<i>But this event is free,
so no tickets will be sold.</i>

14:51.015 --> 14:52.724
<i>According to their official website,</i>

14:52.725 --> 14:55.894
<i>the rooftop food court
will be opening on this day too.</i>

14:55.895 --> 14:58.606
So, although this will be
a live performance event,

14:59.356 --> 15:02.317
I think it's more of a casual setting
where customers can enjoy the show

15:02.318 --> 15:04.153
while having a meal.

15:05.571 --> 15:08.364
Oh, that kind of a show, huh?
Like a traveling theater.

15:08.365 --> 15:10.533
Performers in talks to attend

15:10.534 --> 15:13.411
are local amateurs and indie artists
who are more lenient

15:13.412 --> 15:15.330
with their schedules.

15:15.331 --> 15:17.373
It's basically kind of like

15:17.374 --> 15:19.542
"The Neighborhood Karaoke Competition".

15:19.543 --> 15:21.961
Oh, you'll have nothing to worry about.

15:21.962 --> 15:25.674
What the hell? Karaoke?
Is she trying to make fun of me?

15:27.468 --> 15:31.138
That's how the organizers view this,
but let's prove them wrong.

15:33.557 --> 15:35.976
It's another monster-like Villain!

15:36.477 --> 15:39.687
A combination of "Gigantification",
"Flight", and "Crab" Quirk?

15:39.688 --> 15:42.191
It's a flying monster Villain!

15:44.485 --> 15:45.652
A MAN'S MAN

15:45.653 --> 15:47.445
Hurrah!

15:47.446 --> 15:48.906
Who are they?

15:52.868 --> 15:54.995
Hurrah!

15:55.621 --> 15:57.706
Ahem.

15:58.582 --> 16:00.875
The contrails shining in the sky

16:00.876 --> 16:03.586
are the traces of a man's life.

16:03.587 --> 16:06.547
I'm Captain Celebrity.
It's nice to meet you all.

16:06.548 --> 16:08.466
Hurrah!

16:08.467 --> 16:10.093
Let's cheer, everyone!

16:10.094 --> 16:11.260
Hurrah!

16:11.261 --> 16:12.304
Go, Chris!

16:13.639 --> 16:15.515
Fly, fly!

16:15.516 --> 16:16.641
Fly, Chris!

16:16.642 --> 16:19.060
Big Bro Chris! Hurrah!

16:19.061 --> 16:21.229
We're relying on your strength once more!

16:21.230 --> 16:22.481
Hurrah!

16:23.148 --> 16:25.067
Ah, yes. Hello.

16:26.360 --> 16:30.030
Go, Chris!

16:32.616 --> 16:34.200
Go, Chris!

16:34.201 --> 16:37.787
<i>Look up at the sky...</i>

16:37.788 --> 16:40.581
Here, at Naruhata,
America's top ranking Hero,

16:40.582 --> 16:42.542
Captain Celebrity,

16:42.543 --> 16:45.461
has appeared once again
to defeat a Villain.

16:45.462 --> 16:47.714
His now famous

16:47.715 --> 16:50.968
Japanese-style cheering squad
is gaining even more popularity.

16:51.719 --> 16:53.386
<i>Go, Chris</i>

16:53.387 --> 16:54.887
<i>C.C.</i>

16:54.888 --> 16:57.349
<i>You have a call from Miss Tsukauchi!</i>

16:57.850 --> 16:59.685
- Makoto?
- <i>Hi, Boss.</i>

17:00.477 --> 17:03.104
<i>As you're already aware,
due to the recent damage caused</i>

17:03.105 --> 17:05.606
<i>to downtown Naruhata
by the super gigantic Villain,</i>

17:05.607 --> 17:07.859
<i>things are still not back to normal.</i>

17:07.860 --> 17:11.655
Insurance will be taking care of that,
and I'm helping with the restoration too.

17:12.489 --> 17:14.240
Even now, I'm continuing to prioritize

17:14.241 --> 17:16.617
incidents erupting in the Naruhata area.

17:16.618 --> 17:18.828
I feel like I'm doing all that I can.

17:18.829 --> 17:20.247
<i>I have another good suggestion!</i>

17:20.831 --> 17:24.083
<i>It's an opportunity to significantly
increase your popularity among the locals!</i>

17:24.084 --> 17:25.044
What?

17:26.545 --> 17:29.130
Do what you think is best.
I'll leave everything up to you.

17:29.131 --> 17:31.717
<i>Thank you!
I'll start working on it right away.</i>

17:32.718 --> 17:35.179
Hello. Is this
the Marukane Department Store?

17:35.929 --> 17:37.847
I'm the chief manager
of Captain Celebrity's agency.

17:37.848 --> 17:40.058
My name is Tsukauchi.

17:40.059 --> 17:41.977
May I speak with the event organizer?

17:43.145 --> 17:44.313
Yes.

17:45.189 --> 17:48.316
Yes, we fully support
the objective behind this

17:48.317 --> 17:50.234
proposed project,

17:50.235 --> 17:53.446
so we will not request any payment
on behalf of C.C.

17:53.447 --> 17:56.741
But if you acknowledge and credit him
for his cooperation,

17:56.742 --> 17:58.911
the advertisement
will benefit both of us equally.

17:59.870 --> 18:01.454
For our part,

18:01.455 --> 18:03.915
our goal is to push
the "neighborhood restoration" image.

18:03.916 --> 18:06.334
So, we are in full agreement
with the current plan

18:06.335 --> 18:08.711
to invite local artists to participate
in the event.

18:08.712 --> 18:10.755
But to make sure
it doesn't appear tasteless,

18:10.756 --> 18:13.801
we'd like to consult with you
at a later date regarding the venue.

18:14.468 --> 18:17.845
I believe we will be able to help out
with extra equipment and staff members.

18:17.846 --> 18:19.014
Amazing.

18:21.350 --> 18:24.060
Long story short, I used Boss's name

18:24.061 --> 18:26.522
to make the organizers upgrade the event.

18:27.022 --> 18:29.775
It went from a karaoke competition
to an indie live concert.

18:30.359 --> 18:32.944
We will have to cover the extra costs,

18:32.945 --> 18:34.737
but I'll take care of it
with advertising fees.

18:34.738 --> 18:36.948
You're so competent.

18:36.949 --> 18:40.827
I will be taking part in this project
as a representative

18:40.828 --> 18:42.954
of the C.C Agency.

18:42.955 --> 18:45.124
Let's make this event a success!

18:46.291 --> 18:48.084
Thank you.

18:48.085 --> 18:51.379
Oh, and a higher-up
at Marukane Department Store asked

18:51.380 --> 18:52.922
if we wanted to create an ensemble.

18:52.923 --> 18:54.382
Ensemble?

18:54.383 --> 18:56.384
As the highlight of the event,

18:56.385 --> 18:57.927
they want local youths

18:57.928 --> 19:00.347
to sing their theme song.

19:01.974 --> 19:04.600
I think it's a good idea
to garner more attention.

19:04.601 --> 19:07.104
Just listen to the song first.

19:11.733 --> 19:15.194
<i>How's it going, hey hey</i>

19:15.195 --> 19:18.614
<i>Are you doing well, hey hey</i>

19:18.615 --> 19:21.826
<i>Everyone come together</i>

19:21.827 --> 19:25.037
<i>And join us</i>

19:25.038 --> 19:28.749
<i>Did you know, hey hey</i>

19:28.750 --> 19:32.211
<i>Have you heard, hey hey</i>

19:32.212 --> 19:35.382
<i>You can find all sorts</i>

19:35.966 --> 19:39.260
<i>Of good stuff here</i>

19:39.261 --> 19:40.469
- <i>Marukane, Marukane</i>
- Wow.

19:40.470 --> 19:42.472
It sounds like an oldie.

19:43.056 --> 19:44.807
The quality of this song is amazing.

19:44.808 --> 19:46.685
It's simple, yet so profound.

19:47.686 --> 19:49.270
Can I do this song justice?

19:49.271 --> 19:51.940
Plus, I've never collaborated
with other people before.

19:52.733 --> 19:55.860
She says she's not confident,
but she wants to give it a try.

19:55.861 --> 19:58.321
Okay. I'll gather the members

19:58.322 --> 20:00.656
and negotiate with the department store.

20:00.657 --> 20:03.619
You're so competent!

20:05.495 --> 20:06.954
I heard the big news, Pop-san!

20:06.955 --> 20:09.415
You're going to collaborate
with Big Bro Chris!

20:09.416 --> 20:11.834
It's not really a collaboration.

20:11.835 --> 20:15.087
C.C will make an appearance
as the face of the event,

20:15.088 --> 20:18.050
and I'm just going to appear a little
in the "local performance" portion.

20:18.634 --> 20:20.259
So, we probably won't see each other.

20:20.260 --> 20:23.137
That's still amazing.

20:23.138 --> 20:25.640
We'll bring our friends
and watch you perform!

20:25.641 --> 20:26.974
We'll be cheering you on.

20:26.975 --> 20:28.684
Thank you.

20:28.685 --> 20:31.729
But it's my first time performing
on an actual stage,

20:31.730 --> 20:33.607
so I wonder if I'll be able to do it.

20:35.901 --> 20:38.236
Sorry, she's under
a lot of pressure right now.

20:38.237 --> 20:40.238
No need to worry!

20:40.239 --> 20:42.740
Just perform like you always do,
and you'll be fine!

20:42.741 --> 20:44.534
Stop trying to make me feel better!

20:45.035 --> 20:46.578
It's just as I predicted!

20:50.123 --> 20:52.626
Interesting. There's an event, huh?

20:53.210 --> 20:54.962
Sounds like fun.

20:58.090 --> 21:00.967
Huh? What was that?

21:00.968 --> 21:03.720
I guess it doesn't sound like fun.

21:09.601 --> 21:11.561
In fact,

21:12.062 --> 21:14.773
it makes me angry... I think.

21:16.858 --> 21:18.442
Why is that?

21:18.443 --> 21:20.362
Is it that old guy's face?

21:21.488 --> 21:23.282
I don't really know why,

21:23.782 --> 21:27.452
but maybe I should
turn it into a fun event.

21:28.537 --> 21:29.829
Hachisuka!

21:29.830 --> 21:31.915
There you are! I finally found you!

21:32.708 --> 21:36.460
She hasn't been coming to school lately,

21:36.461 --> 21:37.629
but do you know anything?

21:38.297 --> 21:40.841
Nope, I don't know anything.

21:42.259 --> 21:43.302
I see.

21:47.472 --> 21:48.724
Found you.

21:51.810 --> 21:54.438
Glad to see you're doing well.

23:27.197 --> 23:29.740
<i>There's a power outage during the event.</i>

23:29.741 --> 23:31.450
<i>I had no clue</i>

23:31.451 --> 23:33.703
<i>what Master was planning to do.</i>

23:34.287 --> 23:35.580
<i>Or who he was fighting against.</i>

23:36.498 --> 23:38.916
<i>Next time, "The Day Of."</i>

23:38.917 --> 23:40.459
<i>Place all emotions inside the fist.</i>

23:40.460 --> 23:42.003
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
